implementation_plan.md

# Tuning codegen intermediates — derived from TUNABLES.md, regenerated every run.
/tools/tuning_codegen/*.json

# `> /dev/null` on Windows. Git Bash resolves it; cmd and PowerShell do not, so a
# redirect from either writes a literal "dev/null" file at the repo root — or a
# "dev/null/" directory, when something copies into it. A worktree here collected
# four git hooks that way, and they were untracked and unignored, one `git add -A`
# from being committed.
#
# Narrow on purpose: "/dev/" would silently swallow a real dev/ folder if anyone
# ever adds one, and this project has enough silent things in it already.
/dev/null
/dev/null/
